---
// ROOFFUL INSTANT-QUOTE TAB — PLACEMENT RESERVED, NOT INTEGRATED (team call, 2026-08-18).
//
// ⚠ THERE IS NO EMBED CODE YET. This renders the right-edge tab and nothing behind it. It does not
// load a script, does not open a panel, and does not promise an instant quote — because a button
// that says "Instant Quote" and then does nothing is worse than no button, and the live WordPress
// site already had exactly that: a header CTA pointing at /instant-roof-quote/, a page that does
// not exist and is not being built.
//
// WHERE THE EMBED DROPS IN. Roofful supplies either a <script> tag or an iframe URL. Neither goes
// in this file:
//
//   1. The script tag belongs in BaseLayout, before </body>, as `is:inline` — the same treatment
//      the reveal and market-select scripts get, so it is not deferred behind a bundle.
//   2. This component keeps the tab and gains the click handler that opens whatever Roofful gives
//      us — a panel, a modal or a redirect.
//   3. Delete `data-needs="roofful-embed"` when it is wired, and the punch-list grep stops
//      reporting it.
//
// UNTIL THEN THE TAB IS INERT AND SAYS SO. It is a plain link to the estimate page, which is the
// honest version of the same promise: a real quote from a person who has looked at the roof. When
// the embed lands, that href becomes the fallback for anyone whose JavaScript did not run.
//
// It is deliberately NOT rendered on the estimate pages themselves — a floating tab pointing at the
// page you are already on is noise.
import { estimateHref } from "../data/markets.js";
const { market } = Astro.props;
---
<a
  class="roofful-tab"
  href={estimateHref(market)}
  data-needs="roofful-embed"
  aria-label="Get a free estimate"
>
  <span class="roofful-tab-txt">Free Estimate</span>
</a>
